==Battleground==
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
*1 [[Selena]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As always, meatshielding non-stop and whittling down Selena with [[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|Backliners]] is the key to victory. However, the flood of peons renders [[:Category:Single Attack Cats|Single Attack]] units such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]] significantly less effective, so use [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] or [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] as your primary means of defense instead.

[[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]] can be helpful, especially if she manages to [[Freeze|freeze]] Selena, but don't expect her to survive for long. Be careful not to knock back Selena too much, or else your cats might walk straight into Director Kurosawah's range.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Never Not Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Not Summer!]] stages, Lazy Tomorrow's Japanese name, Natsu no Jō-san ("Summer Mr. Joe"), is a reference to a song, in this case "[https://youtu.be/TBzqcsaT3K0 Natsu no Ojō-san]" ("Summer Girl") by [[wikipedia:Ikue Sakakibara|Ikue Sakakibara]].
**It is the only Never Not Summer! stage to reference a song from the 1970s rather than the 90s.

